concepts=[
C('Your Brain at 1:17 A.M.','COMEDY + SLEEP LITERACY','A stick figure negotiates one last scroll with a tiny courtroom version of their own brain, then turns the joke into a practical wind-down experiment.','At 1:17 a.m., my brain scheduled a meeting about a video of a raccoon.','Make bedtime easier: park the phone away from the bed, set a stop cue, and test a repeatable wind-down routine. General habit advice, not a medical fix.','What ridiculous thing has your brain called urgent after midnight?','Your brain at 1:17 a.m. (the meeting could have been an email)',N(('0:00-0:07','At 1:17 a.m., my brain scheduled a meeting about a raccoon opening a lunchbox. The agenda: watch seventeen more videos.'),('0:07-0:16','I said, We need sleep. My brain said, Counterpoint: what if the raccoon has a sequel? It had slides.'),('0:16-0:27','That endless next clip is easy to follow because there is no natural stopping point. Don’t make bedtime depend on winning a debate with a tiny lawyer.'),('0:27-0:39','Change the setup: choose a stop time, charge the phone out of arm’s reach, and pick a calm replacement, like a paper book or quiet audio.'),('0:39-0:50','The goal isn’t perfect discipline. It’s fewer decisions when you’re tired. My brain has appealed. The phone is charging in the hallway.'),('0:50-0:56','What has your brain called urgent after midnight?')), [S('Court summons','Sleepy figure sees glowing phone; tiny gavel-shaped notification appears.','Close-up of recurring protagonist at bedside, dramatic teal night light, glowing phone with abstract icons, tiny paper summons slips into foreground, comic courtroom framing, 2D editorial vector, no text.','Paper summons slides into frame as camera gently pushes toward phone; figure turns head then freezes. Preserve black-line design; one simple action.','Soft phone ping; tiny wooden gavel tap.','1:17 A.M. / EMERGENCY: RACCOON VIDEO'),S('The negotiation','Tiny courtroom brain presents ridiculous evidence as figure tries to leave.','Wide bedroom; same host faces desk-sized brain courtroom and comically tall stack of blank video cards, midnight blue and orange, no typography.','Tiny brain judge raises one card; stack wobbles but stays upright; slow lateral drift, one beat.','Paper shuffle, squeaky chair.','ONE LAST VIDEO becomes seventeen'),S('No stopping point','Conveyor feeds blank video tiles into figure’s lap.','Stick figure beside endless conveyor of blank rounded video tiles looping into darkness, navy/coral infographic, no text.','Tiles glide past; camera tracks belt four seconds, no cuts.','Light ticking rhythm.','No natural stopping point'),S('Change the setup','Character charges phone outside bedroom and leaves book nearby.','Same character puts phone on shelf beyond doorway; book and water by bed, warm lamp, clean line art, no text.','Follow hand placing phone; rack focus to book.','Cable click, page turn.','Make the next good choice easier'),S('Small experiment','Three icons appear: stop cue, distant phone, quiet replacement.','Figure settling into bed; clock circle, phone on shelf, open book icons; mint/indigo background, negative space.','Icons pop one by one; character exhales. Locked camera.','Three soft pops; warm resolve.','Try one small change tonight'),S('Callback','Tiny brain files appeal while character walks away from phone.','Doorway composition matches first scene; host walks from phone shelf, tiny brain holds blank appeal, moonlit palette, loopable framing.','Brain lifts card; camera pushes toward phone and ends on opening framing.','Quiet gavel tap.','What was urgent at 1 A.M.?')], 'Instrumental playful pizzicato and muted marimba over soft lo-fi pulse, 94 BPM, sleepy midnight curiosity, comic staccato accents on meeting/raccoon joke, reassuring warm resolution, sparse under voice, no vocals, no imitation.'),
C('The Pub Bill That Split the Table','COMEDY + ADULT HARM REDUCTION','A group bill becomes a cartoon geometry problem. Split equally is a choice, not an obligation; a safe ride home is part of the plan.','The bill arrived. Suddenly everyone became a mathematician.','Agree on payment before ordering. Set a spending limit, pace drinks with water/food, and arrange a sober ride. No one needs to justify not drinking.','What is your group’s most chaotic bill rule?','The pub bill: one table, twelve calculators',N(('0:00-0:07','The bill arrived. Suddenly everyone became a mathematician. I had two fries, but they were emotionally shared.'),('0:07-0:16','One wants equal split. One had soda. One ordered a mountain of snacks and says they were for the table.'),('0:16-0:27','The awkwardness isn’t arithmetic. Nobody agreed on the plan before ordering. A thirty-second check-in can save twenty minutes of detective work.'),('0:27-0:39','Decide whether to split equally or pay for what you ordered, set a comfortable spending limit, and plan the ride home before the night starts.'),('0:39-0:50','If you drink, pace yourself, eat, and alternate with water. If you don’t drink, that’s a complete sentence. The calculator is off duty.'),('0:50-0:56','What is your group’s most chaotic bill rule?')), [S('The bill lands','Receipt rolls as everyone reaches for calculators.','Adult stick figures at non-branded pub table; oversized blank receipt unrolls, amber/plum palette, no alcohol labels or text.','Receipt rolls toward camera; three hands reach for calculators; gentle push-in.','Receipt flutter, calculator beeps.','THE BILL HAS ENTERED THE CHAT'),S('Snack forensics','One points at fries; another presents tiny evidence crumb.','Fries and crumb arranged like evidence, two debating figures, flat shapes, no brands or words.','Pan fries to crumb; one points, other raises tiny magnifier.','Magnifier twinkle.','I HAD TWO FRIES'),S('Three payment styles','Three payment approaches shown as icon panels.','Three panels with stick figures and abstract coins: equal, itemized, settle later; no symbols or text.','Panels highlight left to right with scale pulse.','Three muted clicks.','Agree on the method first'),S('Plan before ordering','Group agrees on plan before next order.','Friends at table; one gestures to blank notepad with plate, coin, car icons; everyone nods, no logos.','Nods in sequence; tilt from notepad to faces.','Chatter dips; pencil tap.','Budget + payment + ride'),S('Safety plan','Sober friend gestures toward ride as another chooses water.','Two adults beside water glass and simple car icon; supportive gesture, warm streetlight, nonjudgmental, no text.','Water slides forward; friend points to car icon.','Pour; indicator click.','Choose a safe ride before you go'),S('Punchline close','Calculator becomes tired referee as bill is settled.','Tiny calculator with blank referee whistle shape, friends smiling, coin tokens, amber palette; loop to receipt.','Calculator tilts; receipt rolls back into frame matching opening.','Whistle squeak.','What is your table’s rule?')], 'Instrumental bouncy lounge funk, muted bass, brushed snare, plucky keys and handclaps, 104 BPM, sociable comic energy, pause at bill reveal, responsible warm ending, no vocals.'),
C('Read the Room Is Not Consent','SERIOUS + RELATIONSHIP EDUCATION / ADULTS','A confident stick figure misreads ambiguous signals; a friend explains that uncertainty is a cue to ask and consent must be freely given and ongoing.','A green light in your imagination is still…your imagination.','Consent is clear, voluntary, specific, and can change. Ask plainly, listen without pressure, and stop if answer is no, uncertain, or someone cannot freely choose. Educational reminder, not legal advice.','What makes it easier to ask a respectful question?','The room cannot answer for someone',N(('0:00-0:07','A green light in your imagination is still… your imagination. Our hero mistook a smile for a signed contract.'),('0:07-0:16','A smile can mean hello, nervousness, politeness, or I recognize that song. Guessing doesn’t tell you what someone wants.'),('0:16-0:27','A better move is simple: ask. Would you like to kiss? Then give the other person room to answer honestly.'),('0:27-0:39','Consent should be freely given, specific, and ongoing. A yes to one thing isn’t yes to everything. No, pause, or uncertainty means stop and check in.'),('0:39-0:50','Respect isn’t a mood-killer. It helps both people choose the moment. Our hero replaced mind-reading with words.'),('0:50-0:56','What makes it easier to ask a respectful question?')), [S('Imaginary green light','Host sees green light inside thought bubble.','Two adult figures in neutral social setting; host imagines green light in thought bubble while other gives ordinary wave; clearly separate thought/reality, nonsexual vector, no text.','Thought bubble inflates; focus shifts from imagined signal to ordinary wave; non-intimate body language.','Sparkle then record-stop.','A guess is still a guess'),S('Ambiguous signals','Icons show different meanings of a smile.','Adult figure smiles politely; icons of greeting, nerves, music, recognition, no words, minimal palette.','Icons appear one by one; zoom out.','Four soft pops.','One signal can mean many things'),S('Ask plainly','Host asks openly and leaves space.','Two adults at comfortable conversational distance, open palm, visible exit and personal space, neutral art, no text.','One hand gesture then wait; still camera.','Music lowers; room tone.','Ask. Leave room for an answer.'),S('Ongoing and specific','Separate choice gates with pause icon.','Three separate choice gates and pause symbol; figures comfortable, navy/teal/gold, no text.','Gates light individually; pause appears last.','Three clicks; pause chime.','Specific. Freely given. Ongoing.'),S('Respect the answer','Host accepts no and steps back kindly.','Adult figure gives stop palm; other nods and steps back, no shame or threat.','Listener nods and steps back; wide calm camera.','Warm note.','No, pause, or unsure means stop'),S('Better connection','Both characters chat comfortably.','Same adults chatting with space and empty speech bubble; balanced, reassuring, no text.','Bubble briefly forms question mark then circle.','Room tone and chime.','Respect makes room for both')], 'Instrumental gentle lo-fi piano, soft brushed percussion, warm pads, 82 BPM, thoughtful and reassuring, no sensuality or drama, room under speech, pause after question, warm resolution, no vocals.'),
C('Trust Is Not a Password','SERIOUS + RELATIONSHIP LITERACY / ADULTS','After a fictional adult couple faces a breach of trust, a character reaches for surveillance as shortcut. Repair needs accountability and mutually chosen boundaries, not forced monitoring.','If trust needs a password audit every hour, the password isn’t the problem.','Repair, if both want it, needs honesty, accountability, time, and boundaries both accept. Surveillance or coercion is not proof of trust. Seek support if conversations feel unsafe.','What action shows accountability better than a promise?','Can a password repair trust?',N(('0:00-0:07','If trust needs a password audit every hour, the password isn’t the problem. Meet two fictional adults after a serious breach.'),('0:07-0:16','One offers every login. It sounds like a shortcut. But checking a phone can’t manufacture honesty or erase hurt.'),('0:16-0:27','Repair starts by naming what happened, answering reasonable questions honestly, and taking responsibility without blaming the person hurt.'),('0:27-0:39','Both decide what boundaries they need and whether rebuilding is right. Boundaries are choices; surveillance demanded through fear is control.'),('0:39-0:50','Trust, if it returns, comes from consistent actions over time. A promise is a beginning. The next honest choice is evidence.'),('0:50-0:56','What action shows accountability better than a promise?')), [S('Password shortcut','Character offers oversized key; partner uncertain.','Two fictional adults in calm living room; one offers giant blank key with lock icon, other looks hurt, muted blue/rust, no details.','Key slowly grows between them; restrained expressions.','Low soft piano.','A password cannot erase harm'),S('The audit loop','Phone becomes a loop of repeated checks.','Metaphorical phone with circular blank checkmarks; adults separated, no readable UI.','Loop rotates once while characters stay still.','Repetitive tick then stop.','Monitoring is not repair'),S('Name and own it','One listens without deflecting.','Adult listens openly while other speaks; broken bridge icon, warm background, no blame gestures.','Speaker gestures; listener nods and lowers shoulders.','Room tone; warm music.','Accountability starts with honesty'),S('Choose boundaries','Each places a marker, leaving space.','Two adults each place own boundary marker; respectful gap, bridge pieces nearby but unjoined.','Markers appear separately; camera eases back.','Two wood taps.','Boundaries are each person’s choice'),S('Consistent actions','Bridge rebuilt one plank at a time.','Calendar squares and small bridge repaired; adults only if both choose, green/gold, no text.','One plank settles; calendar turns.','Wood click.','Trust takes time and evidence'),S('Open ending','Two characters at fork; rebuilding is optional.','Two adults at fork; path to bridge and path to separate safe exits equally lit, no forced reunion.','Pull back to reveal both paths; bridge key silhouette recalls opening.','Calm unresolved chord.','Repair is a choice, not a demand')], 'Instrumental restrained felt piano and soft synth-cello pad, 72 BPM, humane and reflective, no villainizing, romance or suspense, low dynamics, calm unresolved finish, no vocals.'),
C('The Urgent Delivery Message','COMEDY + DIGITAL SAFETY','A stick figure nearly gives a one-time code because a message says a parcel is stuck. Verify through official channel; never share authentication codes.','Your parcel is held hostage. The ransom? A six-digit code.','Unexpected OTP, PIN or payment requests are a red flag. Don’t share codes or use message links. Open the official service independently and contact support through a trusted channel.','What do you check first when a message creates panic?','The parcel can wait. Your OTP should stay private.',N(('0:00-0:07','Your parcel is held hostage. The ransom? A six-digit code. It says urgent, which is exactly why we slow down.'),('0:07-0:16','Our hero expects socks. A text claims a delivery fee is due and asks for a one-time password. The socks hired suspicious lawyers.'),('0:16-0:27','A one-time code can prove it’s you during sign-in or payment. Someone asking you to read or send it is a red flag.'),('0:27-0:39','Don’t click the link or call the number in the message. Open the official delivery app or website yourself. Never share an OTP, PIN, or password.'),('0:39-0:50','If you shared a code, contact the real service or bank promptly through its official channel and secure the account. Socks can stay in witness protection.'),('0:50-0:56','What do you check first when a message tries to create panic?')), [S('Ransom note','Blank alert and sock parcel under spotlight.','Stick figure at home, abstract alert and sock parcel under theatrical spotlight, playful mystery, no text/brand.','Alert bounces; spotlight swings from phone to parcel.','Ping and suspense pluck.','URGENT IS A REASON TO PAUSE'),S('Suspicious request','Six-dot code floats toward lock but hand stops it.','Six abstract dots near generic lock; open hand pauses them, no digits/text.','Dots drift and stop at palm.','Brake squeak then silence.','Never share a one-time code'),S('What code does','Icons show temporary key proving identity.','Person, temporary key token, generic account door; no words or brands.','Icons illuminate in order.','Three clicks.','The code can unlock access'),S('Verify independently','Character opens generic service icon, dismissing message.','Stick figure opens generic service icon from clean home screen; no realistic UI or logos.','Message slides away; service icon opens.','Swipe and chime.','Open the official app yourself'),S('If already shared','Character contacts service and secures account.','Calm figure uses support phone icon and closed shield over account, no text/panic.','Shield closes; figure breathes.','Shield click.','Act through a trusted channel'),S('Socks in witness protection','Parcel wears detective hat; protagonist points at viewer.','Sock parcel with tiny detective hat, protagonist points at viewer, soft light, loops to opening.','Hat tips; spotlight returns.','Comic sting.','Would you trust this message?')], 'Instrumental light mystery-comedy with muted pizzicato strings, soft pulse and marimba, 98 BPM, alert not frightening, brief stop on code warning, reassuring witty finish, no vocals.'),
C('Your Paycheck Has Tiny Leaks','COMEDY + EVERYDAY MONEY LITERACY','Paycheck arrives in a bucket; subscriptions, fees and impulse buys spring tiny leaks. The character uses a no-shame audit and waiting rule.','My paycheck didn’t vanish. It escaped through six tiny subscriptions.','Review transactions, label recurring charges, cancel what you don’t value, and wait before nonessential purchases. General budgeting education, not personalized financial advice.','Which recurring charge surprised you most?','The tiny leaks in your paycheck',N(('0:00-0:07','My paycheck didn’t vanish. It escaped through six tiny subscriptions and a delivery fee wearing a fake moustache.'),('0:07-0:16','Each charge looked small alone. Together they formed a tiny leak committee that met monthly without inviting me.'),('0:16-0:27','Check the last month of transactions. Mark recurring charges and ask: Would I choose this again today?'),('0:27-0:39','Cancel what you don’t value, keep what you do, and try a one-day wait before nonessential purchases. A budget is a plan, not punishment.'),('0:39-0:50','Move a small amount toward a goal you choose, if your situation allows. The leak committee is replaced by a boring spreadsheet.'),('0:50-0:56','Which recurring charge surprised you most?')), [S('Leaky bucket','Coins drip through small holes with icons.','Figure holds bucket of blank coins leaking through screen, delivery and shopping icons, mint/coral, no currency or logos.','Three coins drip; tilt down.','Three plinks.','Small charges add up'),S('Leak committee','Subscription icons meet around calendar.','Screen, box and music note icons around blank calendar; host watches, no labels.','Icons stamp calendar in sequence.','Stamp taps.','They meet every month'),S('Transaction audit','Character reviews rows and circles repeats.','Abstract ledger rows and repeating icons; magnifier, text omitted.','Magnifier glides down rows; repeats glow.','Paper slide.','Review one recent month'),S('Choose again today','Character sorts icons into keep and cancel baskets.','Two baskets with check/pause symbols; calm sorting, bright colors, no text.','One icon goes in each basket.','Basket thumps.','Keep what you still value'),S('Add waiting rule','Shopping icon waits beside one-day clock.','Shopping bag icon and sun-to-moon clock; protagonist waits calmly, no brands.','Clock rotates halfway; bag still.','Two ticks; chime.','Pause before nonessential buys'),S('Committee adjourns','Icons leave; bucket stops leaking.','Steady bucket, plan card with symbols, tiny icons march away, echoes first image.','Icons exit; coin lands; opening angle returns.','Coin plink.','What would you choose again?')], 'Instrumental clean lo-fi groove with muted bass, soft snaps, plucky synth and marimba, 96 BPM, practical optimism, comic tiny-leak accents, clear narration space, no vocals.'),
C('The Scroll That Ate the Bus Stop','COMEDY + ATTENTION LITERACY','A stick figure misses a stop because a scrolling feed becomes a tunnel. Explain unpredictable rewards plainly and offer user-controlled boundaries.','I opened one short video and arrived in a different postcode.','Continuous content and unpredictable rewards can make stopping hard. Try a timer, disable autoplay where available, put the phone away during one chosen activity, and notice what helps. No shame or diagnosis.','What boundary helps you get your attention back?','One video later: wrong bus stop',N(('0:00-0:07','I opened one short video and arrived in a different postcode. The bus driver has started charging rent.'),('0:07-0:16','Each swipe might bring something funny, useful, or forgettable. The unpredictable next reward can make one more tempting.'),('0:16-0:27','That doesn’t mean you have no self-control. The feed has no natural ending, so you can add one.'),('0:27-0:39','Set a timer, turn off autoplay if available, or put the phone away during one activity you want to enjoy.'),('0:39-0:50','Try one change for a week. The goal isn’t to hate your phone; it is to choose when you’re done.'),('0:50-0:56','What small boundary helps you get your attention back?')), [S('Wrong stop','Character looks up at an unfamiliar stop.','Figure on bus absorbed by phone; window scenery passes to unfamiliar stop, no text/logos.','Scenery slides; character looks up; pan to stop.','Bus whoosh; music stop.','ONE VIDEO LATER'),S('Unpredictable tiles','Abstract feed tiles alternate bright and dull.','Phone represented by colorful blank tiles; thumb hovers; no UI/text.','Tiles flip irregularly; thumb pauses then moves.','Uneven soft plucks.','The next swipe is a surprise'),S('No ending','Endless tiles loop around figure.','Friendly infographic loop of blank rounded tiles around stick figure.','Tiles move; camera pulls back to reveal no end.','Looping soft beat.','Feeds can keep going'),S('Add stopping point','Character sets timer and turns off generic autoplay toggle.','Timer icon and generic toggle, no brand/text.','Timer appears; toggle moves once.','Click and chime.','Make your own stopping point'),S('Phone away','Phone rests in bag while character walks with friend.','Two figures outdoors, phone in bag, trees and sun, relaxed, no text.','Track walking pair; one wave.','Bird chirp.','Protect one moment you choose'),S('Choice and callback','Character pockets phone before feed opens.','Bus-stop composition; protagonist pockets phone as bus arrives, echoes opening.','Phone slides away; bus arrives; return to opening glow.','Bus chime resolves.','When do you want to be done?')], 'Instrumental gentle bouncy lo-fi electronic groove, 92 BPM, repeated curious plucks suggest loop, never frantic, pause midway, warmer acoustic texture on phone-away beat, no vocals.'),
C('The Screenshot Needs a Passport','COMEDY + MEDIA LITERACY','A dramatic screenshot travels through a group chat like a rumor with a fake passport. Check source, date and context before forwarding.','This screenshot has no source, no date, and a very confident font.','Find the original source, check date/context and seek independent confirmation. If unverified, don’t forward as fact. Avoid shaming friends.','What is your kindest way to pause a rumor?','A screenshot needs a source and a date',N(('0:00-0:07','This screenshot has no source, no date, and a very confident font. The group chat promoted it to breaking news.'),('0:07-0:16','By the fourth forward, everyone knows someone who knows someone. The screenshot has a passport but no origin.'),('0:16-0:27','Before sharing a surprising claim, find the original source. Check when it was published and whether it was cropped out of context.'),('0:27-0:39','See whether credible independent sources confirm it. If you can’t verify, pause instead of forwarding it as fact.'),('0:39-0:50','You can say, I’m not sure this is current. Does anyone have the source? That protects the chat without embarrassing the sender.'),('0:50-0:56','What is your kindest way to pause a rumor?')), [S('Confident screenshot','Blank card in tiny tie enters group chat.','Group-chat metaphor: blank screenshot card in tiny tie at podium, generic bubbles, no text/logos.','Card straightens tie and steps to podium; push in.','Microphone tap.','CONFIDENT FONT, ZERO SOURCE'),S('Rumor passport','Card collects forwarding stamps; source slot blank.','Blank card with abstract stamps and globe; empty source outline.','Three stamps land; pan to empty source.','Stamp thumps.','More forwards do not prove it'),S('Find origin and date','Character traces image to source and calendar.','Magnifier follows link chain to blank source document and calendar, no words.','Magnifier sweeps screenshot to source to date.','Detective pluck.','Find original + check date'),S('Check context','Crop expands to show wider image and surrounding text-like lines.','Frame expands around neutral image and blank lines, demonstrating context without claim.','Frame expands smoothly once.','Paper unfold.','Could context change meaning?'),S('Independent sources','Distinct document icons show possible confirmation.','Three generic documents, two matching checks and one uncertain; no outlet names or claims.','Icons appear one by one; checks illuminate.','Two soft clicks.','Look for independent confirmation'),S('Polite pause','Character asks chat for source without accusation.','Friendly chat; blank question bubble and screenshot card steps aside, warm palette, echoes first scene.','Bubble moves center; card steps back; loop to podium.','Send sound.','Pause the forward, keep friendship')], 'Instrumental playful newsroom marimba, muted bass and brushed percussion, 100 BPM, curious not sensational, stamp accents, spacious source-check pause, friendly resolution, no vocals.'),
C('The Friend Who Needs a Way Out','SERIOUS + NIGHTLIFE SAFETY / ADULTS','A friend feels uncomfortable at a crowded venue. Another uses low-drama options: check in, offer distraction, find staff/security, or call a trusted ride.','The best rescue plan might sound like: Come help me find my jacket.','Check privately what the person wants. Offer choices, involve trained staff or trusted friends, arrange a safe ride. In immediate danger contact local emergency services.','What low-drama code phrase would your friends agree on?','A quiet exit plan can help',N(('0:00-0:07','The best rescue plan might sound like, Come help me find my jacket. No confrontation. Just a friend opening a door.'),('0:07-0:16','At a crowded venue, someone with you looks uncomfortable and says they want to leave. Check privately what they want.'),('0:16-0:27','Offer choices: walk to a quieter area, find venue staff/security, call a trusted friend, or arrange a ride.'),('0:27-0:39','A distraction can help if they want it. Don’t pressure them to explain or confront someone if that could make things less safe.'),('0:39-0:50','Stay together while planning. In immediate danger, get staff help and contact local emergency services.'),('0:50-0:56','What low-drama code phrase would your friends agree on?')), [S('The signal','One friend discreetly signals another at busy venue.','Adult stick figures at music venue, soft abstract lights, discreet signal, no alcohol focus/logos.','Hand lifts; friend notices and turns; subtle tighten.','Low crowd, cue chime.','A quiet signal is enough'),S('Private check-in','Friends move to quieter edge and check what would help.','Two adults at quiet venue edge, space, attentive listener, visible exit, no text.','Listener leans slightly but keeps distance; steady camera.','Crowd lowers.','Ask what would help'),S('Offer choices','Icons show quiet area, staff, trusted friend and ride.','Four simple support icons around pair, no brand/words.','Icons light one at a time.','Four clicks.','Offer options, let them choose'),S('Distraction','Friend asks help finding a jacket and they walk toward exit.','Adult friend gestures to coat-check; other agrees; exit visible, non-confrontational.','Both walk together, side-track.','Footsteps; muffled music.','A simple excuse can open space'),S('Get support','Friends talk to staff and arrange a ride.','Two friends with generic trained staff near lit entrance; phone ride icon, no branding.','Staff gestures to bright area; friend confirms ride.','Door chime.','Use staff or trusted support'),S('Safe exit','Friends leave together to pickup area.','Two adults walking to well-lit pickup, night palette echoes opening.','Follow toward light; motif returns to opening.','Footsteps fade.','Make a plan with your people')], 'Instrumental warm ambient pulse, soft synth pad, muted hand percussion, 78 BPM, supportive not panicked or clubby, duck under speech, gentle lift at safe exit, no vocals.'),
C('Sorry You Felt That Way Is Not a Repair','COMEDY + COMMUNICATION SKILLS','A stick-figure apology comes in a gift box with only a sorry you felt that way balloon. A simple repair formula turns it useful.','This apology contains one balloon, zero responsibility.','A useful apology names the action, recognizes impact, takes responsibility without but, and offers a concrete change. The other person owes no immediate forgiveness.','What phrase makes an apology feel real to you?','The apology with zero responsibility',N(('0:00-0:07','This apology contains one balloon, zero responsibility. The card says, Sorry you felt that way. The balloon is doing all the work.'),('0:07-0:16','Repair starts by naming what you did, not grading how the other person reacted.'),('0:16-0:27','Try: I interrupted you in the meeting. That dismissed your point, and I’m sorry. No but you were… hiding in the bushes.'),('0:27-0:39','Then say what you’ll change: Next time I’ll let you finish. A real apology offers action, not a demand for instant forgiveness.'),('0:39-0:50','The other person gets time to decide what they need. Our balloon has been reassigned to the party department.'),('0:50-0:56','What phrase makes an apology feel real to you?')), [S('Balloon apology','Gift box opens; sad balloon rises as character points proudly.','Meeting room figures; gift box has limp balloon, listener puzzled, kind comic vector, no text.','Balloon rises; tilt to listener.','Box pop, squeak.','ONE BALLOON, ZERO OWNERSHIP'),S('Name action','Host sees interruption as a replay.','Meeting metaphor with overlapping blank speech bubbles and replay icon.','Speech overlaps; replay circles once.','Soft rewind.','Name what you did'),S('Recognize impact','Idea card falls behind table.','Blank idea card slides as person tries speaking; protagonist notices.','Card slides; posture shifts to listening.','Paper slide.','Recognize the impact'),S('Take responsibility','Character offers open speech bubble and listens.','Two facing figures, one open bubble, no defensive gestures, warm palette.','Speaker nods; listener has space; still camera.','Music softens.','No but attached'),S('Offer a change','Turn-taking token sits on table.','Meeting table, turn-taking token, calm figures, forward arrow and blank calendar.','Token slides to center and rests.','Wood click.','Offer a specific next step'),S('Balloon reassigned','Balloon is party decor while conversation continues.','Balloon tied to party box; calm conversation, echoes first scene.','Balloon bobs; return to gift-box frame.','Squeak resolves.','Forgiveness is not owed on demand')], 'Instrumental light quirky piano and muted pizzicato bass, 90 BPM, conversational comedy with empathy, soft plucks at apology formula, no triumph, room for example, no vocals.')]

story=[Spacer(1,18*mm)]
cover=Table([[P('PANELFLOW / SHORTS LAB','CoverEyebrow')],[P('10 stick-figure<br/>video concepts','CoverTitleX')],[P('A production-ready prompt pack for short, useful, entertaining explainers','CoverBody')],[P('<b>Format</b> Vox-inspired editorial stick-figure animation<br/><b>Length</b> 45-56 seconds<br/><b>Pipeline</b> MiniMax H3 Image + MiniMax H3 video + Qwen3-TTS + ACE-Step 1.5*','CoverBody')]],colWidths=[176*mm]);cover.setStyle(TableStyle([('BACKGROUND',(0,0),(-1,-1),navy),('LEFTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),14*mm),('RIGHTPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),14*mm),('TOPPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),8*mm),('BOTTOMPADDING',(0,0),(-1,-1),8*mm)]));story += [cover,Spacer(1,10*mm),P('<b>Built for production, not a promise of virality.</b> Each concept uses an honest curiosity hook, a short story, a useful payoff and a real viewer question. Audience response should guide what to make next.','Callx'),P('Prepared 13 November 2026 | Research-led creative brief | Vertical 9:16','Smallx'),PageBreak(),P('How to use this pack','H1x'),P('Treat each scene as an individual short H3 shot, then assemble clips, narration, captions, music and effects in PanelFlow. Six scene beats total 45-56 seconds. Match clip duration to registered H3 graph limits, then trim to narration.','Bodyx')]
for h,b in [('1. Lock the look','Generate a recurring host reference first. Reuse it wherever character reference conditioning is supported. Keep head circle, line weight, proportions and teal scarf consistent.'),('2. Make a still per beat','Use each image prompt for one keyframe. Add title and caption lettering in post, never in generated artwork.'),('3. Animate simply','Feed each keyframe to H3 video with its one-action prompt. Simple movement helps preserve the drawn character.'),('4. Build the sound','Generate instrumental beds; mix below Qwen narration. Add listed SFX manually. The music model is not asked to create SFX.'),('5. Review','Check consistency, timing, readability, intelligibility, factual accuracy and safety before export.')]:story.append(P('<b>'+h+'</b><br/>'+b,'Bodyx'))
story += [P('Shared image prompt prefix','H2x'),P('Append to each scene prompt: Vertical 9:16 educational explainer; Vox-inspired editorial stick-figure animation, original generic visual language; recurring protagonist: black circular head, thin consistent limbs, small teal scarf, expressive pose; crisp black outlines, flat limited palette, geometric backgrounds, high contrast, readable silhouette, negative space for captions added later; coherent 2D vector-like illustration; no photorealism, 3D, logos, watermarks, readable text, extra limbs or clutter.','Promptx'),P('Reuse the host reference wherever the image workflow supports it. Keep neighboring keyframes close in character scale and camera distance.','Bodyx'),P('Shared H3 video prefix','H2x'),P('Animate supplied keyframe as clean 2D editorial stick-figure explainer. Preserve exact host, props, palette and layout. One simple action only, with gentle camera move stated below. Stable line art and flat shapes; no morphing, new people/objects, cuts, readable text, dialogue or soundtrack. End on a stable frame. Append each scene motion direction.','Promptx'),P('Shared Qwen3-TTS voice direction','H2x'),P('English, warm bright adult explainer voice, conversational and precise, lightly witty on comic lines, calm/respectful on sensitive topics; natural Indian English accent if supported; clear consonants, 145-155 words/minute, varied emphasis and short pauses; no shout or influencer exaggeration. Read supplied text verbatim; add no words. Generate per timed beat if needed, then join.','Promptx'),P('Audio mix','H2x'),P('Narration stays clearly in front; duck music; place brief SFX at marked beats. Burn captions inside the mobile safe area. Use rights-cleared audio.','Bodyx'),P('*The brief said DSC Step 140. This pack assumes ACE-Step 1.5, the closest verifiable model name. Confirm PanelFlow’s exact registered ID before generation. Prompt captions may need syntax changes for the installed build.','Callx'),PageBreak(),P('What the research suggests','H1x'),P('No reliable recipe guarantees virality. Platform guidance points toward clear openings, compact stories, expectation match, community interaction and iteration from actual audience data. These are craft choices, not algorithm hacks.','Bodyx')]
for h,b in [('Start with the moment','YouTube Shorts guidance highlights first-second hooks and compact bits that tell a mini-story. Open on a concrete oddity, then satisfy it.'),('Match title and opening','YouTube Analytics measures viewers still watching after 30 seconds and suggests testing changes when an intro underperforms. Deliver the title promise.'),('Invite discussion','Instagram creator guidance covers creation, engagement, reach and guidelines. End with a real question, without demanding a share or follow.'),('Make value memorable','One takeaway and one visual metaphor per video. Humor earns attention then yields to clarity; serious subjects stay human, not sensational.'),('Review and iterate','Compare similar-length uploads. Review opening, dips, spikes and comments after data arrives. A spike can mean rewatch or confusion.'),('Ethical retention','Use curiosity that gets resolved. Don’t withhold safety info, fabricate cliffhangers, exploit fear, promise outcomes or encourage compulsive use.')]:story += [P(h,'H2x'),P(b,'Bodyx')]
story += [P('Pilot plan','H2x'),P('Make three pilots from comedy, practical safety, and relationship/communication. Keep style consistent; change one major variable at a time. Use channel retention and comments/shares to choose what to develop, comparing with your own recent videos.','Callx'),PageBreak()]
for i,c in enumerate(concepts,1):
 story += [P(f'{i:02d} / {escape(c["title"])}','H1x'),P(escape(c['tag']),'H2x'),P('<b>Premise.</b> '+escape(c['prem']),'Bodyx'),P('<b>Hook.</b> '+escape(c['hook'])+'','Callx'),P('<b>Takeaway.</b> '+escape(c['take']),'Bodyx'),P('<b>Suggested title.</b> '+escape(c['card']),'Bodyx'),P('Narration script','H2x')]
 for tm,line in c['narr']:story.append(P('<b>'+tm+'</b> &nbsp; '+escape(line),'Bodyx'))
 story.append(P('Scene prompts / one keyframe + one short H3 clip per beat','H2x'))
 for j,(name,beat,img,vid,sfx,cap) in enumerate(c['scenes']):story += [P(f'Scene {j+1} | {escape(name)} | {c["narr"][j][0]}','SceneX'),P('<b>Visual:</b> '+escape(beat),'Smallx'),P('<b>MiniMax H3 Image:</b> '+escape(img),'Promptx'),P('<b>MiniMax H3 video:</b> '+escape(vid),'Promptx'),P('<b>Caption:</b> '+escape(cap)+' &nbsp; <b>SFX:</b> '+escape(sfx),'Smallx')]
 story += [P('Qwen3-TTS direction','H2x'),P('Use shared voice direction. '+('Lightly amused at setup; soften on takeaway; never sneer at the person.' if 'COMEDY' in c['tag'] else 'Measured, empathetic, direct; avoid melodrama.'),'Bodyx'),P('ACE-Step 1.5 music prompt','H2x'),P(escape(c['music']),'Promptx'),P('<b>End question:</b> '+escape(c['cta']),'Bodyx'),P('Check narration/caption sync, cut on visual beats, keep effects sparse, inspect for accidental text, and review sensitive-topic accuracy.','Smallx')]
 if i<len(concepts):story.append(PageBreak())
story += [PageBreak(),P('Upload and learning checklist','H1x')]
for q in ['First frame presents premise immediately; no logo intro.','Opening line and title promise the same thing.','One clear idea; advice includes limits.','Stick-figure design and palette remain consistent.','No accidental text, brands or unsafe generated details.','Captions legible on phone and clear of UI.','Voice intelligible; music below; SFX matched.','Sensitive scenes show adults, consent, agency and safety.','No guaranteed results or misleading shock framing.','Review retention and compare similar-length uploads before changing one major element.']:story.append(P('-  '+escape(q),'Bodyx'))
